IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tel-types`

-- Telecommunications Act 2001 — GOAL 3: THE LEVY.
--
--   "What interest is due on a levy paid late?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2001_103.txt — s 14.

§ `Goal 3 — the levy`

-- s 14 "(1) If any service provider liable to pay the levy fails to pay the
-- whole amount ... by the date specified ..., the service provider must pay
-- interest on the unpaid amount at the rate of 1.5% per month calculated from
-- the date payment is due. (2) Interest will be calculated in monthly
-- instalments for each month, or part of each month, that the payment is
-- due." Months run from the due date; a payment after the due date in month k
-- (or on its last day) counts k months; simple interest on the unpaid amount
-- (fork F3).
@ref s 14(1)-(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Levy payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months of levy interest for` p MEANS
    IF   p's `levy paid on` AT MOST p's `levy due on`
    THEN 0
    ELSE count 1
    WHERE
        GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        count k MEANS
            IF   p's `levy paid on` AT MOST `add months` (p's `levy due on`) k OR k AT LEAST 1200
            THEN k
            ELSE count (k PLUS 1)

@ref s 14(1)-(2)
@export The interest on levy paid late under s 14 of the Telecommunications Act 2001 (NZ): 1.5% of the unpaid amount for each month, or part of a month, from the due date to payment. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Levy payment`  @desc The due date, the unpaid amount and the payment date
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on late levy` p MEANS
    0.015 TIMES p's `levy unpaid` TIMES `the months of levy interest for` p
